<title>HONG KONG: Hong Leong aims to merge hotel subsidiary - paper.</title>
<headline>Hong Leong aims to merge hotel subsidiary - paper.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-09-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Hong Leong group is aiming to merge its Hong Kong listed unit CDL Hotels International with a luxury hotel chain to raise its international profile, a Hong Kong newspaper reported on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Potential suitors in the US$100 million deal were likely to include the Regent, Fairmont and Hilton hotel groups, the South China Morning Post reported.</p>
<p>CDL, which runs 55 hotels with 14,500 rooms worldwide, would be able to tap management resources of its future partner and improve earnings, the paper said.</p>
<p>Company spokesmen were not immediately available for comment.</p>
<p>--HONG KONG NEWSROOM (852) 28436441</p>
